        "On the first Saturday of every month, a community hall in a small northern town fills with broken things. A woman carries in a toaster that no longer heats; a boy arrives with a bicycle whose gears slip; an elderly man sets down a radio that has been silent for a year. Around the room, volunteers sit at long tables covered with screwdrivers, sewing machines and soldering irons. This is a “repair café,” and its rules are simple: repairs are free, but you must stay and watch, and if possible, help.",
